   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The table lists the wins in order from largest to smallest. There are 30 data values.</p>\n<p>Suppose you have a set of data with <i>n</i> values, ordered from the smallest to the largest. If <i>n</i> is odd, the median is the data value at position <span data-math=\"\\frac{{n + 1}}{2}\"></span>. If <i>n</i> is even, then add the values at the <span data-math=\"\\frac{n}{2}\"></span> and <span data-math=\"\\frac{n}{2} + 1\"></span> positions, then divide by 2 to find the median.</p>\n<p>Since there are 30 data values, use the even method.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{n}{2} = \\frac{{30}}{2} = 15\"></span> and <span data-math=\"\\frac{n}{2} + 1\"></span>= 16</p>\n<p>The 15<sup>th</sup> value is 81 and the 16<sup>th</sup> value is 84.</p>\n<p>Add them up and divide by 2: <span data-math=\"\\frac{{81 + 84}}{2}\"></span>= 82.5</p>\n<p>The median is 82.5.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "82.5"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
